title: Exodus from the Banners
subtitle: Owing to its militarization, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] [? if not lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed and not lvp_leave_banner: and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] are leaving the Banners.
view-if: banner_militancy >= 0.2 and not banner_exit and not banner_stay and not lvp_leave and not concord_formed
new-page: true
tags: event
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/reichsbanner_flag.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= Exodus from the Banners

The Banners has become increasingly militarized as of late, with ever-greater quantities of arms and paramilitary training, as well as a stream of <span style="color: #9B0000;">radicalized</span> <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> members. In response, the members associated with the other Unity parties, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] [? if not lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed and not lvp_leave_banner: and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?], are threatening to leave for good. They signed up for a mass movement to defend the republic, not a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> militia.

- @let_go: Let the <span style="color: #000000;">centrists</span> [? if not lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">liberals</span>?][? if lvp_formed and not lvp_leave_banner: and <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span>?] go.
- @lower_militancy: We must lower the Banners's militancy.
- @keep_them: Can we convince them that a militant Banners is necessary for defending the Republic?

@let_go
on-arrival: banner_strength *= 0.9; unionist_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 5; banner_exit = 1; left_strength += 5*(1-dissent); ddp_right += 3; lvp_right += 3

We have judged that the Banners's militancy is more important than maintaining a coalition with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] [? if not lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed and not lvp_leave_banner: and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]. The Banners members affiliated with these parties leave, while the left of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> is strengthened.

# TODO: this should make it harder to form Commonwealth coalitions


@lower_militancy
on-arrival: banner_militancy *= 0.5

Bowing to the other parties' demands, we reduce the Banners's military training, thus inducing them to stay.


@keep_them
unavailable-subtitle: They are unable to be convinced at this time.
choose-if: strife >= 5 and (unionist_relation >= 50 or unionist_leader == "Stilling" or (unionist_leader == "Hawkins" and unionist_relation >= 30)) and ((ddp_relation >= 50 and not lvp_formed) or (lvp_relation >= 50 and lvp_formed))
on-arrival: banner_stay = 1; ddp_left += 2; ddp_cohesion += 2; lvp_left += 2

Seeing the strife that has filled the Commonwealth's streets, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] [? if not lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed and not lvp_leave_banner: and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] seem to be convinced that it is necessary for the Banners to be militarized, and will not leave the organization.